    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0179" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg179"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Welles to Mr. Seward</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy
                            Department</hi>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-10-24"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">October</hi> 24,
                    1861</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 19th instant and enclosures, and to transmit herewith a
                    copy of a report of Captain William W. McKean, commanding United States ship
                    Niagara, and a copy of a report of Commander Melancton Smith, which contain such
                    information as the department possesses in relation to the seizure of the
                    British ship “Perthshire” by the United States steamer Massachusetts, and her
                    subsequent release by order of Captain McKean.</p>
                <p>I am, respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>GIDEON WELLES.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d109-a1.xml" xpointer="d109-a1"/>
